# This file is written automatically by the installer wizard -- you
# shouldn't normally need to edit it by hand. Documented here for
# reference/troubleshooting, and for anyone running the agent manually
# (e.g. `node local-agent.js`) without the installer.

# The exact name of the Windows-registered printer this agent sends
# labels to -- selected from a live dropdown during install (Get-Printer),
# never free-typed, so it always matches exactly.
PRINTER_NAME="DYMO LabelWriter 4XL"

# Which local port to listen on. Optional -- defaults to 17631, chosen
# to avoid common local dev server ports. The installer always writes
# this same default; only change it by hand if 17631 happens to
# conflict with something else already running on this specific
# machine (and if you do, the Ovenette app's own print button is
# hardcoded to 17631 too -- see src/lib/print-agent-client.ts in the
# ovenette repo -- so the two need to be changed together).
# PORT="17631"
